{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-149459","model_call":54,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2298"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2298"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_94142915#1_185117954","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2298","rank":2,"snippet":"over the past year. The discrimination they detail primarily takes the form of verbal harassment, shunning and cyberbullying. The report was released Thursday by the Stop AAPI Hate Youth Campaign, a high school internship program at Stop AAPI Hate, a national center that collects reports of coronavirus discrimination against Asian Americans and Pacific Islanders. The study details the emotional toll of growing anti-Asian sentiment around the country. Nearly 8 of 10 respondents expressed anger over the epidemic of hate against Asians. The findings come from nearly 1,000 interviews of Asian American young adults conducted by a team of 87 Asian American high school <cover>students this summer. Full coverage of the coronavirus outbreak \"I think we hear this a lot, but the youth are the future,\" said Cassie Eng, a senior at the Urban School of San Francisco, who worked on the study. \"\" , \"start_char\": 826.000000 , \"title\": \"'You have Chinese virus!': 1 in 4 Asian American youths experience racist bullying, report says\" , \"url\": \"https://www.nbcnews.com/news/asian-america/25-percent-</cover>asian-american-youths-racist-bullying-n1240380\" }"},"time":9},"model_calls":54,"document_judgments":20,"relevance_3":5,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
