{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-149459","model_call":82,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2256"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2256"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_234038487#1_620331035","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2256","rank":13,"snippet":"Why You Should Not Bully People Bullying In Laurie Halse Anderson's Speak Bullying in Schools The Effects Of Media Violence On Society Satire Essay On Bullying In Schools \" , \"segment\": \"35% of kids have been threatened online and six out of ten teenagers say they witness bullying in school every day. 75% of school shooting incidents have been linked to bullying and harassment. Verbal bullying is the most common type of bullying, with about 77 <cover>percent of all students being verbally bullied in some way including mental bullying or verbal abuse. These types of bullying can also include spreading rumors, yelling obscenities or other derogatory terms based on an individual's race, </cover>gender, sexual orientation and religion. Nearly nine out of ten youth reported being verbally harassed at school in the past year due to their sexual orientation. It is estimated that 160,000 children miss school every day due to fear of attack or intimidation by other students. One of every ten students who drop out of school do so because of repeated bullying. Bullying is associated with serious health concerns. Children frequently involved in bullying as bullies or as victims share a ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_96954426#1_230628919","rank":9,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_587897128#0_1288358716","rank":10,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_96954426#2_230631256","rank":11,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_1043879213#10_2155808690","rank":12,"relevance":2}]},"time":6},"model_calls":82,"document_judgments":26,"relevance_3":11,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
